  "id": "repertoire",
  "term": "repertoire",
  "definition": "Repertoire refers to a grouped body of works or styles used for comparison within a performance domain, such as Baroque, Romantic, or late Romantic music. In this context, repertoire means the category of material being performed, allowing differences in expressive behavior to be examined across stylistic groupings.",
